buffer_cache: upload CPU writes onto GPU-written pages instead of downloading them

From Lichii PR 103 (merge 3165a2b6f, head cb3ea0d7d0) by Zarigis, unchanged. It applied
as it stands.

WriteMemory kept GPU-written bytes that share a page with a CPU write by downloading
the page, which finishes the scheduler and waits for the GPU. Ocarina does this about
230 times a second, and it kept the split's back thread waiting 60% of the time. For
Switch 2 titles the CPU's bytes now go into the buffer through
InlineMemoryImplementation, as CachedWriteMemory does, and nothing waits. Ranges no
buffer covers still download. MemoryManager::WriteBlock now invalidates after its copy,
and first cancels pending downloads over the range through PrepareRegionWrite, because
the inline path uploads from guest memory.

EDEN_NX2_INLINE_PAGE_WRITES=0 restores the download, =1 forces the upload.

Measured with 0092 by FabianZettl (issue 589, RX 7800 XT, RADV, Ocarina): frame time
37-55 ms became 21-31 ms.

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index 679bf92d6..52f3c7b92 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -191,6 +191,20 @@ void BufferCache<P>::WriteMemory(DAddr device_addr, u64 size, bool keep_page_gpu
     const DAddr page_begin = Common::AlignDown(device_addr, DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
     const DAddr page_end = Common::AlignUp(device_addr + size, DEVICE_PAGESIZE);
     if (keep_page_gpu_data && gpu_modified_ranges.Intersects(page_begin, page_end - page_begin)) {
+        // Switch 2 titles: upload the CPU's bytes into the buffer instead, as CachedWriteMemory
+        // does, so the page stays GPU-owned and nothing waits for the host GPU.
+        static const int forced = [] {
+            const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_INLINE_PAGE_WRITES");
+            return value == nullptr ? -1 : (value[0] == '0' ? 0 : 1);
+        }();
+        const bool inline_writes =
+            forced >= 0 ? forced == 1 : Tegra::g_nx2_ampere.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        if (inline_writes && IsRegionRegistered(device_addr, size)) {
+            tmp_buffer.resize_destructive(size);
+            device_memory.ReadBlockUnsafe(device_addr, tmp_buffer.data(), size);
+            InlineMemoryImplementation(device_addr, size, tmp_buffer);
+            return;
+        }
         DownloadMemory(page_begin, page_end - page_begin);
     }
     memory_tracker.MarkRegionAsCpuModified(device_addr, size);
